auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  # OAuth scope access tests (ONEROSTER-28)

  Each subfolder requests an LEA token limited to one OneRoster scope and checks which
  endpoints that token can reach. Per the OneRoster 1.2 Rostering spec (section 4.3.3):

  - `roster.readonly` or `roster-core.readonly` grants every endpoint except `demographics`
  - `roster-demographics.readonly` is the only scope that grants `demographics`
  - a missing scope returns HTTP 403 in the `imsx_*` error envelope

  The scope URIs are collection variables (`scopeRoster`, `scopeRosterCore`,
  `scopeRosterDemographics`) defined in `collection.bru`. Each subfolder stores its token
  in its own environment variable so the full-scope `lea-odsApiToken` used by the other
  folders is not overwritten.
}
